  "profiles": [
    {
      "id": "nzta_7A8",
      "pattern": "^7A8",
      "segments": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "end": 3,
          "key": "assigning_authority",
          "values": {
            "7A8": "NZ transport authority"
          },
          "source_ids": [
            "nzta"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "documented",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "start": 4,
          "end": 5,
          "key": "make",
          "values": {
            "DH": "Nissan"
          },
          "source_ids": [
            "nzta"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "documented",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "start": 6,
          "end": 7,
          "key": "model_code",
          "values": {},
          "source_ids": [
            "nzta"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "documented",
          "note": "LANDATA model lookup unavailable; 6L must not be split into a model-year digit and batch letter."
        },
        {
          "start": 8,
          "end": 9,
          "key": "vehicle_type_code",
          "values": {
            "01": "Mopeds[1]",
            "02": "Trailers and trailer caravans",
            "03": "Tractors[1,2]",
            "04": "Agricultural machines[1,2]",
            "05": "Trailers not designed for normal highway use[1]",
            "06": "Mobile machines not designed for normal highway use[1]",
            "07": "Passenger cars and vans",
            "08": "Goods vehicles (vans, utilities, trucks)",
            "09": "Passenger vehicles (buses)",
            "10": "Self-propelled caravan",
            "11": "Motorcycles",
            "12": "All-terrain vehicles (ATVs)[3]",
            "13": "Special purpose vehicles[2]",
            "23": "Agricultural tractors capable of more than 50km/h"
          },
          "source_ids": [
            "nzta",
            "nzta_virm_attributes"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "documented",
          "note": "The positions come from NZTA's pre-2009 VIN diagram, which prints 07 in this slot and captions it \"NZTA vehicle type code\"; the code meanings come from VIRM 2-2 Table 2-2-1, quoted verbatim including its superscript note markers. Only the pre-2009 layout has this slot: the post-2009 layout replaces it with the meaningless X at position 9. The register records its own wording for 13 of these codes in registries/nz.json registry_vehicle_types, keyed by the spelling the register emits; code 23 has no register spelling recorded there, and no correspondence between the two spellings is asserted here."
        },
        {
          "start": 10,
          "end": 11,
          "key": "vin_assignment_year_code",
          "values": {},
          "source_ids": [
            "nzta"
          ],
          "evidence_status": "documented",
          "note": "Two-digit assignment year only; not registration/manufacture year; century unresolved."
        }
      ],
      "note": "The make box in NZTA's pre-2009 diagram holds two characters, \"DH\", while the caption beneath it reads \"0DH denotes Nissan\" -- the three-character form the post-2009 diagram uses. The box and its own caption disagree, and the box is the layout, so DH is recorded for positions 4-5. The discrepancy is the source's, and is carried here rather than resolved silently.",
      "unconstrained_fields": {
        "description": "Fields NZTA prints without stating any format rule. Recorded so the absence of a check is deliberate and attributable: the decoder reads these as written and enforces nothing, because a rule the publisher never stated would reject VINs the register may legitimately carry.",
        "vin_assignment_year_code": "NZTA prints \"Year the VIN assigned\" with the examples 01 and 09, and states no rule that the code is numeric.",
        "serial_component": "NZTA prints \"Number derived from the last six digits of the OE chassis number or randomly derived if no chassis number or VIN already exists\", with the example 123456, and states no rule that the result is numeric.",
        "note": "What the source does state is enforced, and only that: NZTA writes that a valid VIN \"consists of 17 characters that never contain the letters I, O or Q\" (VIRM 1-1 VIN and chassis number), and diagram 2 prints \"No meaning always X\" at position 9."
      }
    },
