      "note": "The registration authority assigns this VIN itself, so its characters carry no manufacturer variant and no production year. Declared here rather than in code so that a register whose authority assigns VINs under a different prefix, or not at all, states its own.",
      "authority_assigned_prefix": "7AT",
      "authority_label": "NZTA",
      "unconstrained_fields": {
        "description": "Fields NZTA prints without stating any format rule. Recorded so the absence of a check is deliberate and attributable: the decoder reads these as written and enforces nothing, because a rule the publisher never stated would reject VINs the register may legitimately carry.",
        "vin_assignment_year_code": "NZTA prints \"Year the VIN assigned\" with the examples 01 and 09, and states no rule that the code is numeric.",
        "serial_component": "NZTA prints \"Number derived from the last six digits of the OE chassis number or randomly derived if no chassis number or VIN already exists\", with the example 123456, and states no rule that the result is numeric.",
        "note": "What the source does state is enforced, and only that: NZTA writes that a valid VIN \"consists of 17 characters that never contain the letters I, O or Q\" (VIRM 1-1 VIN and chassis number), and diagram 2 prints \"No meaning always X\" at position 9."
      }
